---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CORRECTIONS_EMAIL } from '../site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Editorial policy"
  description="How pulse360 chooses sources, uses AI, attributes reporting and handles corrections."
  updated="October 16, 2026"
>
  <h2>Our standards</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Accuracy first.</strong> A brief may only state what the reporting outlets stated. If the reporting is too thin to summarize, we don't publish.</li>
    <li><strong>Attribution.</strong> Claims are credited to the outlet that reported them, and every brief links to its sources.</li>
    <li><strong>Neutrality.</strong> We don't editorialize, take political positions or write sensational headlines.</li>
    <li><strong>No duplication.</strong> When several outlets cover the same event, we publish one brief that draws on all of them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Sources</h2>
  <p>
    We monitor a fixed list of established news organizations: international wire
    services, public broadcasters, national newspapers and recognized specialist
    publications. Sources are weighted by reliability, and more credible outlets carry
    more weight in what we choose to cover. We don't use anonymous blogs, social media
    posts or press releases as sole sources.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of AI</h2>
  <p>
    pulse360 uses an AI language model to draft its briefs from the source reporting.
    The model works under fixed instructions:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>use only facts contained in the source material;</li>
    <li>attribute claims to the outlet that reported them;</li>
    <li>don't speculate, predict or add commentary;</li>
    <li>decline to write a brief when the source material is insufficient.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    AI can still make mistakes. That is why every brief links to the original reporting,
    and why we act on corrections quickly. Every article carries a note saying it was
    produced with AI assistance.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If you find a factual error, email <a href={`mailto:${CORRECTIONS_EMAIL}`}>{CORRECTIONS_EMAIL}</a>
    with the article link and what is wrong. We review every report. Confirmed errors
    are corrected, and briefs that cannot be corrected are removed.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>
    pulse360 isn't affiliated with any of the outlets it summarizes. Advertising,
    if shown, is served by third-party networks and has no influence on which
    stories we cover or how they are summarized.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
